description:
(3) species name (in some cases, identification to Genus or Family may be acceptable);
Atlantic Blue Crab Callinectes sapidus
(4) Phylum, Class, and Order to which species belongs;
Phylum Arthropoda, Class Malacostraca, Order Decapoda
(5) key morphological traits used to identify individual (within Order);
The immovable, fixed finger of the claws is blue with red tips
(6) Functional/ecological ‘fun fact’ about taxa.
Males and females can be easily distinguished by the shape of the abdomen (known as the "apron”).
